ular to the first principal component in which the data varies the most.\n\nIn our diagram, the direction where the variance changes the most corresponds (approximately) to the vector $\\mathbf{b},$ as shown below. So, $\\mathbf{b}$ defines the direction of the first principal component.\n\n![](images/2b/2b4539ab239ecf0e54d5e828079469b928dd9201ae5aa913db13104bf1ed1796.png)\n\n   \n\nNext, notice that in the 2D case, we have only one direction perpendicular to the first principal component. And this direction corresponds to the vector $\\mathbf{c},$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/a3/a3d1e84cc1a20da39af058b422ea7860a11eb97c0afa59be752b0ca3ed0a14be.png)\n\n  \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$\\mathbf{c}$ only.\""} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f6314eaa-c493-5b5e-8488-3575762a00e0" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184511 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6e62c25-4776-554e-9307-f8b4d4fa48c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$b$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186181243} {:answer/id #uuid "d570afc9-7186-5929-925b-a96f76356e6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$c$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186181244} {:answer/id #uuid "fb926b50-2053-5742-9cad-cef3204bc978" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a$ and $c$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186181245} {:answer/id #uuid "0c418500-bfb3-553e-a665-c08e321bd536" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$b$ and $c$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186181246} {:answer/id #uuid "4cfb308d-96b2-5026-a5d8-d118e722e4d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186181247}] :answer-field/id #uuid "a9697911-7b88-5d07-95e8-c0bda27abb52" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186181242}] :question/id #uuid "a785b327-9818-57fc-833b-de8abc79a02f" :question/math-academy-id "q-148159" :question/problem "![]