The *second principal component* of the data corresponds to the direction perpendicular to the first principal component in which the data varies the most.\n\nIn our diagram, the direction where the variance changes the most corresponds (approximately) to the vector $a,$ as shown below. So, $a$ defines the direction of the first principal component.\n\n![](images/9c/9c4f0dc8899f5c9c5a9007d867c4bedbf6510849996bcd875117c2c28784be04.png)\n\n \n\nNext, notice that in the 2D case, we have only one direction perpendicular to the first principal component. And this direction corresponds to the vectors $b$ and $c,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/d1/d1e3a31906faf6f8a3b6f811de95bec362d51eb8a6212e73269e64f7d07726fb.png)\n\n  \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$b$ and $c$ only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186514376 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99ecb2af-34f8-57f1-8b34-71e60e71947b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$b$ ad $c$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513931} {:answer/id #uuid "a066bebd-7786-58bc-b5b7-aa7face800ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$c$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513943} {:answer/id #uuid "abac1e72-710f-5536-9d71-58caf0e85211" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a$  only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513982} {:answer/id #uuid "abe67997-e5d4-53c3-9912-3aa02e4a053d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$b$  only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513983} {:answer/id #uuid "c29f1158-2be8-578f-a732-30cd6d90b636" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$a$ and $c$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514045}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$b$  only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513983} :answer-field/id #uuid "336057b5-b2ba-5002-aa05-d1f4221fb375" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514246}] :question/id #uuid "1e02af7