{:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426466}] :question/id #uuid "95fd78c2-6907-5df8-b9fe-1452968ce01b" :question/math-academy-id "q-76362" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix\n$L=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{5}{2}\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $L-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nL-\\lambda I=\\begin{bmatrix}0-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{5}{2}-\\lambda \\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(L-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(L-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 2 & \\frac{5}{2}-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (-\\lambda )(\\frac{5}{2}-\\lambda )-2\\cdot 0 & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -\\frac{5}{2}) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =0$ and $\\lambda =\\frac{5}{2}.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are the entries on the main diagonal."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426472 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c33ad59-d29c-5cbd-910f-497a62d62bfe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =3$ and $\\lambda =1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426445} {:answer/id #uuid "7e3b9b16-d329-5f89-9cff-6f464c33458f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-3$ and $\\lambda =1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426449} {:answer/id #uuid "a48e2962-ae97-5ce4-aaf1-eea3d88ff322" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426454} {:answer/id #uuid "e26ddd9b-b057-5d08-b037-5d67a039567e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =-3$ and $\\lambda =-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426461} {:answer/id #uuid "ed7bf537-28bf-51b9-a386-11e70b5bae0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =4$ (double root)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426462}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =3$ and $\\lambda =1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426445} :answer-field/id #uuid "021cb7e9-9e31-5b4e-91d4-a97f82fcb114" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426465}] :question/id #uuid "aaa6413c-ed34-5909-9e88-242b0b85efde" :question/math-academy-id "q-9339" :question/problem "Find all real eigenvalues of the matrix \n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the matrix $B-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nB-\\lambda I=\\begin{bmatrix}3-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1-\\lambda \\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's find and solve the characteristic equation $det(B-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}3-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )-2\\cdot 0 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -3)(\\lambda -1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =3$ and $\\lambda =1.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are the entries on the main diagonal."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186446733 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "311e8f46-648a-5c98-ae9c-c09e69f012d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =\\sqrt{13}$ and $\\lambda =\\sqrt{17}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446648} {:answer/id #uuid "6efd6b7d-bdc0-5be0-b513-c19d0b047800" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =\\sqrt{17}$ and $\\lambda =\\frac{1}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446664} {:answer/id #uuid "84f65cb8-d626-588c-b078-563da250f9ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\lambda =\\sqrt{13}$ and $\\lambda =\\frac{1}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186446673} {:answer/id #uuid "9954f005-4623-5ab9-8eee-41291e4fa96c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "There are no real eigenvalues" :db/id #edb/ref 175921